    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DunVqBBTKyCdoVHcwSbcDf)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- No other open PR touches `sp-see-also` (checked the titles and branches of the 8 open PRs: #427, #421, #420, #419, #418, #415, #171, #125).\n- Merge in any order.\n\n## What it does\n\n- Entries in `*see-also*` and `*see-also-concept*` show the Org tags of the heading they come from as `:a:b:` at the right edge of the entry's heading line.\n- Face `sp-see-also-tags` inherits `org-tag`, so it follows the Modus theme.\n- The tags are a `display` space with `:align-to (- right WIDTH)`, so they stay at the edge when the window is resized.\n- A long title is cut with an ellipsis; the tags never are.\n- `window-configuration-change-hook` redraws the view when the window width changes (folds are lost then).\n- Parser: `sp-see-also--headings` returns `:tags`; mentions carry `:heading-tags`. Cache version 4 to 5, so files are read again once.\n- Only tags written on the heading line; inherited tags and `#+filetags:` are not shown.\n- Literate doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-see-also.org` updated (bullets); `.el` and tests tangled from it.\n- 4 new ERT tests; all 36 pass in Emacs 29.3. The real GUI was not run.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `M-x sp-see-also-show` in a litnote whose footnotes sit under tagged headings: the tags are at the top right of each entry line.\n- [ ] Entries under untagged headings show no tags.\n- [x] Switch between a light and a dark Modus theme: the tag colour follows.\n- [ ] Narrow the window: the title is cut with `…`, the tags stay; widen it again: the title returns.\n- [x] Resize while the window is wide: the tags stay at the right edge.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-see-also-show-concept` shows tags too; RET and clicking on an entry still visit it; TAB, `n`, `p`, `g` still work.\n- [ ] A heading with many tags and a long title: the line does not wrap oddly.\n\n## Revert guide\n\n- `git revert` the merge commit of this PR; nothing else depends on it.\n- Re-tangle `docs/tangles/academic/sp-see-also.org` if you revert by hand.\n- The cache rebuilds by itself (version 5 back to 4).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBM4e5zeN7iHVE1khc)_",
